description: How the project's documents are split and what must stay true
globs: ["*.md", "docs/**/*.md"]
---

The documents are deliberately separate and the instructor requires it:

- `PROJECT_PLAN.md` — scope, milestones, what was deliberately not built
- `TECHNICAL_REPORT.md` — architecture, challenges in STAR format, results
- `CHALLENGES.md` — the same challenges standalone, STAR only
- `README.md` — what it does and how to run it
- `docs/DEMO_GUIDE.md` — VMware setup and a timed three-minute script

STAR means Situation (what the challenge was), Task (what we were doing
previously), Action (what we did), Result (the outcome). Keep that order.

If a code change makes a document wrong, fix it in the same commit. The README
listed a filesystem and a GUI under "deliberately not built" for some time
after both were built.

Counts go stale: self-test checks, shell commands, line counts, file counts.
Verify them rather than copying the old number.

Never claim it has run on real hardware — it has not. Never claim 3D
acceleration works: the driver is complete, but the adapter reports a 3D
hardware version of zero and the driver correctly declines.
